## 3. High-Performance XAML Data Binding & Virtualization

### 3.1 Optimized Virtualizing Controls
For large data sets (>1,000 items), always enforce UI virtualization with container recycling:

```xml
<ListView ItemsSource="{Binding Records}"
          VirtualizingStackPanel.IsVirtualizing="True"
          VirtualizingStackPanel.VirtualizationMode="Recycling"
          VirtualizingStackPanel.ScrollUnit="Pixel"
          VirtualizingStackPanel.CacheLengthUnit="Page"
          VirtualizingStackPanel.CacheLength="2,2"
          ScrollViewer.IsDeferredScrollingEnabled="False"
          ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
    <ListView.ItemTemplate>
        <DataTemplate DataType="{x:Type vm:TelemetryRecordViewModel}">
            <Border Margin="2,1" Padding="8,4" Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceBrush}" CornerRadius="4">
                <Grid>
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding Timestamp, StringFormat='{}{0:HH:mm:ss.fff}'}" 
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Target}" Margin="12,0" 
                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding Status}" 
                               Foreground="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToColorConverter}}"/>
                </Grid>
            </Border>
        </DataTemplate>
    </ListView.ItemTemplate>
</ListView>
```

