## 5. Asynchronous UI & Threading Architecture

1. **Dispatcher Handling:** Use `Dispatcher.InvokeAsync()` only when writing directly to UI-bound elements from non-UI threads.
2. **ConfigureAwait Guidelines:**
   - In Library/Repository code: Always use `ConfigureAwait(false)`.
   - In ViewModel async command handlers: Let execution resume on the UI thread (`ConfigureAwait(true)`).
3. **Progress Reporting:** Use `IProgress<T>` and `Progress<T>` for seamless marshaling back to UI context.

```csharp
public async Task ExecuteLongOperationAsync(IProgress<int> progress, CancellationToken ct)
{
    await Task.Run(() =>
    {
        for (int i = 0; i <= 100; i += 10)
        {
            ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
            Thread.Sleep(50); // Heavy background computation
            progress.Report(i);
        }
    }, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
}
```

